{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19267-gmc-changeling","id":19267,"title":"GMC Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-27T10:59:22-08:00","id":19267,"title":"GMC Changeling","content":"So I'm going to be beginning a mixed campaign, and I was wondering how others have included the GMC update to your changeling games?<br /> Has anyone gone through and made a 'fix' for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T13:11:28-08:00","id":19329,"title":"","content":"I would especially be interested in the EXP costs for Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T05:58:19-08:00","id":19680,"title":"","content":"Here's a chart that I came across, and have brought into the mix for a GMC CtL game.<br /> <i>Merit</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 1 Experience per dot</span></span></span><br /> <i>Skill Specialty</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 1 Experience</span></span></span><br /> <i>Skill</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 2 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <i>Attribute</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 4 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <i>Goblin Contract</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 2 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <i>Affinity Contract</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 3 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <i>Non-Affinity Contract</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 4 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <i>Wyrd</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 5 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <i>Clarity</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 3 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <i>Willpower</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 1 Experience per dot</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1386-thompry","name":"thompry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1386_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T08:37:29-08:00","id":21163,"title":"","content":"Not yet, but I think the &quot;breaking points&quot; mechanic could improve the game experience quite a bit. Instead of asking questions about a character's morality, one would ask questions about how they maintain their sanity and their distinction between what is earthly and what is fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T09:29:41-08:00","id":21179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19267-gmc-changeling?p=21163#post21163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not yet, but I think the &quot;breaking points&quot; mechanic could improve the game experience quite a bit. Instead of asking questions about a character's morality, one would ask questions about how they maintain their sanity and their distinction between what is earthly and what is fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. most people use a modded Integrity as Clarity - add questions about their durance and fetch. and you're basically there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T20:29:23-08:00","id":21429,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys. really helpful, any ideas on on how to add the modded integrity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T06:03:38-08:00","id":21578,"title":"","content":"Uhm, I think i would use the normal integrity system, changing the questions.<br /> <br /> Some ideas:<br /> <br /> &quot;Which one was the worst thing your Keeper did to you?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Which one is the most important memory you have of the mortal world?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What did your keeper stole from you?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Why you don't fit anymore in your old life?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Why you escaped from Arcadia?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What does -home- means to you? &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T19:24:37-08:00","id":25514,"title":"","content":"So i was looking at the price cost and wouldn't it make more sense to have <br /> <br /> <i>Goblin Contract</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 1 Experiences per dot</span></span></span></span><br /> <i>Affinity Contract</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 2 Experiences per dot</span></span></span></span><br /> <i>Non-Affinity Contract</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 3 Experiences per dot</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> My rational is that the cost should be lowered by one experience per dot each because as seen by Dave in the GMC of mage, the costs for ruling, common, and inferior arcanum are 3 4 and 5 respectively.<br /> <br /> Changeling has always had cheaper costs for their affinity and non-affinity contracts than other supernaturals have for their respective magical abilities. <br /> <br /> Just looking for feedback on this logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T22:07:12-08:00","id":26994,"title":"","content":"As a shout-out, Clarity should be 2xp. Humanity is 2xp, so one would assume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T22:58:17-08:00","id":27015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19267-gmc-changeling?p=26994#post26994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a shout-out, Clarity should be 2xp. Humanity is 2xp, so one would assume.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Humanity's expected to be able to fluctuate more wildly than Integrity, I certainly wouldn't mind Clarity being similarly inexpensive to raise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T02:40:32-08:00","id":27085,"title":"","content":"I think that lessening Clarity's cost cheapens it, though, in a bad way. If you make it inexpensive, it takes away the impact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1009-kristastic","name":"Kristastic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1009_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T03:03:17-08:00","id":27094,"title":"","content":"This thread gives us a good idea: to give &quot;flavour&quot; to clarity by changing the conditions which may be applied after clarity rolls.<br /> <br /> Between the ideas i have:<br /> <br /> - Refuse to use changeling magic (-2 penality, or the storyteller may make you fail a contract roll. Or you may forego a contract roll)<br /> <br /> - You convince yourself to be the character of a story (9-again to the roll in theme, -2 to all others)<br /> <br /> - Arcadia calls. On the first option, you go to lose yourself in the hedge.<br /> <br /> - A temporary fraility<br /> <br /> - Your perception breaks. Once, the storyteller may screw up with your senses, also in a knowledge / perception roll.<br /> <br /> - You forgot something about your life pre - kidnapping (the storyteller may introduce the element retroactively, only for critical failure)s<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#2379B5\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/27026-stopgap-werewolf-the-forsaken-gmc-conversion</span></b></span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","user":"Baroqo","date":". 12-10-2013, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T20:44:45-08:00","id":27726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19267-gmc-changeling?p=25514#post25514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i was looking at the price cost and wouldn't it make more sense to have<br /> <br /> <i>Goblin Contract</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 1 Experiences per dot</span></span></span></span><br /> <i>Affinity Contract</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 2 Experiences per dot</span></span></span></span><br /> <i>Non-Affinity Contract</i><span style=\"color:#999999\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 3 Experiences per dot</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> My rational is that the cost should be lowered by one experience per dot each because as seen by Dave in the GMC of mage, the costs for ruling, common, and inferior arcanum are 3 4 and 5 respectively.<br /> <br /> Changeling has always had cheaper costs for their affinity and non-affinity contracts than other supernaturals have for their respective magical abilities.<br /> <br /> Just looking for feedback on this logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went with this for my Changeling game.<br /> <br /> The players loved the cheaper costs of the often punitive Goblin Contracts and I thought it worked pretty well. We don't really have any crossover, but it seems to work pretty well. People are taking contracts and their associated issues as well as running with plenty of merits as per normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T10:35:01-08:00","id":31766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kristastic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19267-gmc-changeling?p=27085#post27085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that lessening Clarity's cost cheapens it, though, in a bad way. If you make it inexpensive, it takes away the impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> Especially since they lessened Humanity's cost, and I do not feel that cheapens it.<br /> If you were to argue that we'd need revised and updated Clarity rules for the lower cost to &quot;feel right,&quot; I'd agree with you.<br /> That said, I'm not making supernaturals pay different costs for their sanity stats across different game lines. That way lies madness (ha).<br /> <br /> I'm using 2 Experiences per entire Goblin Contract, but otherwise using those Contract costs. There was some hearty debate over this on the old forum (much like there was some hearty debate over the cost of Rotes in Mage on the old forum).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T08:59:36-07:00","id":194655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19267-gmc-changeling?p=21429#post21429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks guys. really helpful, any ideas on on how to add the modded integrity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would replace the &quot;What have you forgotten?&quot; question with &quot;What was the worst thing about your Durance?&quot;, something like that. Maybe add &quot;what reminds you of the Fae&quot;, to cover those little things in the old Clarity.<br /> <br /> (And maybe nick B&amp;S's Touchstones, if you want to emphasize Clarity as &quot;ties to reality&quot;.)<br /> <br /> It might be worth looking into hacking Derangements and/or Banes in, somehow - they seem really thematic for Changeling too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T21:07:07-07:00","id":212025,"title":"","content":"Changelings already have banes and derangements, but they are thematically different. How does &quot;Eccentricities and Frailties&quot; sound irrespectively? <br /> <br /> Interestingly, rather than touchstones changelings can have &quot;keystones&quot;. Because everything falls apart when they are removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T19:56:11-07:00","id":228671,"title":"","content":"For an upcoming Changeling game, we're apparently going to implement a condition for when you're under a pledge, and possibly for contracts too. I've never played Changeling myself, so I have absolutely no clue what the words I'm using mean, but my ST seemed to like the idea and it sounded good to me, in theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T21:54:47-07:00","id":228770,"title":"","content":"I think that what really needs to be changed in Changeling is the actual power mechanics. Especially with the GMC rules any powers that deal damage are going to be much, much worse, though Changeling already has the lowest dice pools of any of the splats, despite having so many &quot;per success&quot; abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T00:04:16-07:00","id":228850,"title":"","content":"Mostly you can straight up use GMC rules and slap on Changeling powers. I've yet to run into any major issues in my game that I couldn't arbitrate on the fly. That said, I will warn you that Changelings are rather especially squishy. My players generally fear dying after one, <i>maybe</i> two hits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T06:10:52-07:00","id":229014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19267-gmc-changeling?p=228850#post228850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly you can straight up use GMC rules and slap on Changeling powers. I've yet to run into any major issues in my game that I couldn't arbitrate on the fly. That said, I will warn you that Changelings are rather especially squishy. My players generally fear dying after one, <i>maybe</i> two hits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds fine to me. Most fights shouldn't be to the death, and players dying easy might prompt STs to make sure any fights are actually framed with ulterior motives that differ from &quot;kill the other side completely&quot;. A lot of casual fights you could run into would have to be escalated by someone in order for the combatants to draw weapons or use lethal powers anyway. If that one player who only put points in weaponry and now brawl insists on pulling a weapon every time, he sort of deserves his fights being deadly. 'Course, if there's a lot of monstrous opponents showing up who care little about anything then that might be a different matter, but that's the exception I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T06:30:05-07:00","id":229016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19267-gmc-changeling?p=228850#post228850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly you can straight up use GMC rules and slap on Changeling powers. I've yet to run into any major issues in my game that I couldn't arbitrate on the fly. That said, I will warn you that Changelings are rather especially squishy. My players generally fear dying after one, <i>maybe</i> two hits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I'm going to guess that you don't have any Elementals in your group. Because with the buff armour got in GMC, Contracts of Elements are excellent unaltered and the Elemental Kith bonus makes them increasingly hard to break as their Wyrd climbs. By the end of a long-running Changeling game under the pre-GMC rules I had a player with a Wyrd 8 Elemental and... good grief. He dual-kithed Gargantuan sometime around mid-game, and he could hit 24 health, an armour value in the double digits, and more. Imagine that under the post-GMC rules.<br /> <br /> I mean, that's a ludicrously extreme example that was the result of an unintended combination of a variety of factors that all came together at the end of a long, long game. That said, the Contracts of Elements (well, Clauses 2 and 5 specifically) do become pretty neat in the GMC rules and enable quite tanky Changelings. Then again, that's perfectly appropriate for Elementals I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T14:34:52-07:00","id":229572,"title":"","content":"Hmm, reading the core book now, and it seems like thing such as Beneficent Fate got a big boost in GMC. It gives you 1 hit on an attempted instant action rather than your normal dice roll, so in the old rules (where weapon damage was added to dicepool) it always did 1 damage. Now though, it always does weapon damage + 1 damage. Much better. Defense tends to be higher now too, so being assured a hit is better in and of itself. The real kicker, though, is called shots and Tilts. One of the hardest, and thus most rewarding to pull off, is targeting the eyes. It gets a whopping -5, which combined with an opponent's defense often makes it pretty hard, and can make even shooting with a gun a bit shaky; however, with this power you can instantly take out one of their eyes, no questions asked. Even if you don't really know how to fire a pistol, you can open the fight by shooting one eye out with a heavy pistol (3 lethal damage, -3 to all attacks, halved defense!). That's seriously powerful, even if you can only do it once a day.<br /> <br /> This power also makes Social Maneuvering a breeze; you won't be rolling that more than once a day anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:58:22-07:00","id":229704,"title":"","content":"Just so you know; the Changeling chronicle got confirmed at GenCon. The Huntsmen Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.th